  "email": "mei.chen@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Identify ticket sender and check for obvious account/device issues behind a vague report"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0109",
  "reason": "Check user's laptop for warnings that might explain the vague report"
}

{
  "query": "mailbox full quota",
  "reason": "User's mailbox is at 99.4% which may be the cause of the issue"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for getting in touch. I'm sorry something isn't working. To fix it I need a bit more detail: what isn't working (email, Teams, printing, signing in, VPN, an app)? When did it start? Do you see an error message, and if so, what does it say (a screenshot is great)? I did spot one thing that could be the cause. Your mailbox is about 99% full. Once it fills up, Outlook can stop sending or syncing. If your problem is with email, here's how to free up space: empty Deleted Items and Junk Email, sort your Inbox and Sent Items by size and delete big attachments (or save them to OneDrive first), and move mail older than a year to your Online Archive. The new size can take up to an hour to show. Please reply with the details either way and I'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket is very vague ('it's not working'). lookup_user: account active, no failed sign-ins, not blocked, VPN enabled, password not expiring/forced. Mailbox at 99.4% (50890/51200 MB), so this is a likely cause if the issue is email (KB-010). Laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) is online, checked in recently, 14.6% disk free, no warnings. Gave the user the KB-010 cleanup steps and asked for specifics (what's affected, when it started, error text). No actions queued. If mailbox stays over 95% after cleanup and her role needs more space, escalate for a quota increase (needs manager approval).",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "low"
}
